# ── Planning layer — local only, never committed ──────────────
plans/
TASKS.md
CLAUDE.md
*.backup-*.md

# docs/ is part of the planning layer too. ADRs live on disk beside the repo
# rather than inside it; the reasoning stays private.
docs/

# ── Go ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/bin/
/dist/
go.work
go.work.sum

# ── Wails ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/bin/

# frontend/dist is embedded by main.go via //go:embed all:frontend/dist, so the
# directory must exist for the Go build to compile - keep its placeholder.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/gitkeep

# frontend/wailsjs is generated, but it IS tracked on purpose: App.tsx imports
# it, and the frontend CI job has no Go toolchain to regenerate it with.
# Revisit at Phase 3 - once ipc.ts wraps the bridge behind a mock, the frontend
# stops importing these bindings directly and they can go back to being ignored.

# ── Node / Vite ───────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
# wails dependency-change cache, regenerated on every build
# (a trailing # on a pattern line is NOT a comment - it becomes part of the pattern)
frontend/package.json.md5
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Application runtime data ──────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/logs/
*.log
threadline-snapshots/

# ── Environment & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Editors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Coverage & profiling ──────────────────────────────────────
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
*.pprof

# ── Design canvas exports ─────────────────────────────────────
# Mockups exported from Claude Design. They are a reference for building the
# UI, not part of it: the .dc.html artboards carry inlined assets and a
# support.js runtime that nothing in the app imports. Reference material lives
# beside the repo like the rest of the planning layer.
frontend/Scope section names and mockups/
